Subject: CP-M1: Darwin named FIFO EOF in the existing reactor
Why: Native Darwin probes on two OS versions show a quiet named-FIFO writer close is readable EOF but neither kqueue nor poll signals it. The existing bounded reactor now waits through Rustix unlimited select on its kqueue descriptor and registered FIFOs, preserving critical timers and kicks without threads or timeout polling. Native r57 validates the frozen source, typed invalid-FD refusal, backend fixtures, original two-second coalition/recovery tests, terminal tests and process lifecycle tests.

